<title>GERMANY: E.German July industry output falls 5.5 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>E.German July industry output falls 5.5 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT   July 96    June 96     July 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)  -5.5	 +2.9	  -4.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +3.7	 +5.3	   n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     138.2	146.3	 133.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbnk statistics. Previously reported data in brackets. @</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    July 96	    June 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   148.5	-8.6     162.5	 +3.9</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    185.8	+0.8     184.4	 +2.6</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   120.6     -17.9     146.9	+11.0</p>
<p> Energy output	     90.9	+1.0	90.0	 +0.6</p>
<p> Construction	     200.7	-1.8     204.3	 +2.4</p>
<p>Two month comparison June/July 96 with Apr/May 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +0.5 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison June/July 96 with June/July 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +3.7</p>
<p> Mining					-3.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		   +8.6</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	 +8.1</p>
<p>		Capital goods		+7.9</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	 +12.4</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	    +11.0</p>
<p> Energy output			     +3.2</p>
<p> Construction				-3.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
